# Web3 Authentication and Authorization

Lux provides focused helpers for EIP-4361 Sign-In with Ethereum, session
issuance, role-based access checks, and token-gated access rules.

## SIWE Message

```elixir
alias Lux.Web3.Auth.SIWE

message =
  SIWE.build_message(%{
    domain: "app.example.com",
    address: "0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000",
    statement: "Sign in to Lux",
    uri: "https://app.example.com/login",
    chain_id: 1,
    nonce: "AbC12345",
    issued_at: DateTime.utc_now() |> DateTime.to_iso8601(),
    expiration_time: DateTime.utc_now() |> DateTime.add(300, :second) |> DateTime.to_iso8601()
  })
```

Parse and validate the message:

```elixir
{:ok, parsed} = SIWE.parse_message(message)

:ok =
  SIWE.validate_message(parsed, %{
    domain: "app.example.com",
    chain_id: 1,
    now: DateTime.utc_now()
  })
```

Signature verification is intentionally injectable so applications can use the
wallet/signing stack they trust:

```elixir
verifier = fn message, signature, opts ->
  # Recover the address with your configured Ethereum signature library.
  {:ok, opts[:expected_address]}
end

SIWE.verify_signature(message, signature, %{
  verifier: verifier,
  expected_address: parsed.address
})
```

## Sessions

```elixir
alias Lux.Web3.Auth.Session

session =
  Session.issue(parsed.address, %{
    roles: [:member],
    permissions: [:read_signals],
    ttl_seconds: 3_600
  })

Session.expired?(session)
```

## RBAC

```elixir
alias Lux.Web3.Auth.RBAC

policy = %{
  admin: [%{action: :*, resource: :*}],
  member: [%{action: :read, resource: :signals}]
}

RBAC.authorized?(session, :read, :signals, policy)
```

## Token Gates

```elixir
alias Lux.Web3.Auth.TokenGate

holdings = %{
  {1, "0xa0b86991c6218b36c1d19d4a2e9eb0ce3606eb48"} => 150_000_000
}

rules = [
  %{
    chain_id: 1,
    contract: "0xA0b86991c6218b36c1d19D4a2e9Eb0cE3606eB48",
    min_balance: 100_000_000
  }
]

TokenGate.allowed?(holdings, rules)
```

## Security Notes

- Generate nonces server-side, store them, and mark them used after successful login.
- Always validate domain, chain id, expiration, and nonce before issuing a session.
- Keep signature recovery in a dedicated adapter so the application can pin a reviewed Ethereum library.
- Store sessions server-side or sign/encrypt them with application-level key rotation.
- Evaluate token gates server-side from trusted indexer/RPC data, not client-submitted balances.
